0s"Hornworts & Thallose liverworts" Plant without distinct leaves. 011113505
0 Plant with distinct leaves011213602
0s"Leafy liverworts" Leaves arranged either strictly in 2 ranks or in 3 ranks (one on each side of the stem and one in mid-ventral line) ; the leaves most commonly round or 2-lobed, without nerves (sometimes leaves are so deeply divided as to appear 4- or 5-ranked. 0223147024
0 Leaves not arranged strictly in ranks (except in Fissidens and Distichium, which have nerved leaves, and Schistostega, which has a shining green protonema) ; the leaves never 2-lobed, most often tapering to an acute or rounded tip, with or without nerves022414803
0 Plants consisting of numerous upright stems on which branches are in groups arranged spirally down the stem ; all grow in bogs or wet ground, and look pale when dry, but are vivid green, orange-brown or purple-red when moist, and hold water like a sponge 03451590Sphagnum0
0 Plants never showing the regular, whorled branching of Sphagnum ; habits and habitats various0346151004
0s"Acrocarpous mosses" Separate, upright or ascending shoots which are simple, forked, or with a few short lateral branches ; leaves very seldom like thin, glossy scales ; seta arising from tip of shoots (except in some species of Fissidens, Racomitrium, etc.). The acrocarp/pleurocarp split may appear difficult at first. Looking at the gallery of images on pp. 9-18 may help. 04671611078
0s"Pleurocarpous mosses" Mat-like growth of much-branched stems, which are irregularly intertwined and most often prostrate or arched ; branching most often irregular or pinnate (occasionally growth is upright from a horizontal stolon, branched above to give plant a miniature tree habit, e.g. Climacium) ; leaves most often like thin, glossy scales ; seta not arising from tip of stems. The acrocarp/pleurocarp split may appear difficult at first. Looking at the gallery of images on pp. 9-18 may help. 046816120285
0 Thallus with gemmae in very obvious receptacles0519171306
0 Thallus without gemmae in receptacles05110171408
0 Gemmae visible in open-topped receptacles ; no gemmae on thallus tips ; upper surface of thallus with raised pores06911181507
0 Gemmae hidden in receptacles like flasks with a long neck ; thallus tips with star-shaped gemmae on the surface; upper surface of thallus without raised pores 0691218160Blasia pusilla0
0 Gemmae in cup-shaped receptacles 07111319170Marchantia polymorpha0
0 Gemmae in crescent-shaped receptacles 07111419180Lunularia cruciata0
0 Upper surface of thallus with polygonal markings ; a more or less raised pore in centre of each polygon081015201909
0 Upper surface of thallus without such markings and pores0810162020011
0 Thalli usually > 1 cm wide ; plants strongly scented ; pores on upper surface easily visible to naked eye ; scales on lower surface not overlapping each other 09151721210Conocephalum spp.0
0 Thalli always < 1 cm wide ; plant scentless ; pores on upper surface hardly visible to naked eye ; scales on lower surface overlapping one another0915182122010
0 Diamond-shaped marking prominent ; thallus tastes peppery ; young female heads dull green and 4-lobed 010181922230Preissia quadrata0
0 Diamond-shaped markings very faint ; thallus not peppery to taste ; young female heads bright green and with 5-7 lobes 010182022240Reboulia hemisphaerica0
0 Plants growing in pale green rosettes on bare soils, or floating in pools01116212325012
0 Plants deep or vivid green ; habit various01116222326015
0 Upper surface of thallus with round-topped cells and a spongy appearance ; on wet mud 012212324270Riccia cavernosa0
0 Upper surface of thallus with flat-topped cells, or some round-topped cells, not appearing spongy01221242428013
0 Thallus narrow, forming mats of Y-shaped plants ; either floating or on periodically flooded mud 013242525290Riccia fluitans0
0 Thallus with sort, wide branches, plants ± forming rosettes ; on soil01324262530014
