0 Hairs restricted to margins and underside of plant01731342938018
0 Narrow shoot tip with abundant gemmae ; tip sticking away from substrate 018343530390Metzgeria fruticulosa/M. temperata0
0 Shoot tip usually without gemmae (occasionally a few) ; tip not narrower than rest of thallus, not sticking away from substrate 018343630400Metzgeria furcata0
0 Midrib well-defined (obvious when viewed from underside of thallus)01930373141020
0 Midrib not well-defined01930383142023
0 Thallus with narrow, forking branches at the tip 020373932430Pellia endiviifolia0
0 Thallus without forking branches at the tip02037403244021
0 Plant monoicous (female part in a flap on upper side of thallus ; male parts in small volcano-like hollows on same thallus ; non-fertile plants should be recorded as Pellia sp.) 021404133450Pellia epiphylla0
0 Plant dioicous (female part in a short tube on upper side of thallus ; male parts in small volcano-like hollows on separate thallus ; non-fertile plants should be recorded as Pellia sp.)02140423346022
0 Female plants with tubes that have fringed mouths 022424334470Pellia endiviifolia0
0 Female plants with tubes that have mouths which are slightly wavy 022424434480Pellia neesiana0
0 Plants vivid mid-green, with a greasy appearance ; thalli parallel-sided ; margins curved upwards ; fertile parts on thallus sides ; capsules egg-shaped, held on a colourless seta 023384535490Aneura pinguis0
0 Plant forming dark green rosettes ; margins not curved upwards ; fertile parts in pits on upper surface ; capsules long, horn-like and green 023384635500Anthoceros spp./Phaeoceros spp.0
0 Leaves divided into 2 unequal lobes, the smaller one lying more or less flat on or under the larger one, thus sometimes giving impression that leaves are in 4 ranks0243473651030
0 Leaves not divided into 2 unequal lobes, may be 2-toothed0243483652025
0 Leaves irregular, wavy, not distinctly separated from each other or from the stem ; appearance like a small lettuce02548493753026
0 Leaves in regular rows and quite distinct from stem02548503754027
0 Plant pale or dark green ; rhizoids purple ; on soil (only identifiable to species using spores – collect ripe, black capsules) 026495138550Fossombronia spp.0
0 Plant bright green ; rhizoids pale ; in dune slacks 026495238560Petalophyllum ralfsii0
0 Leaves split into many finely divided parts, sometimes appearing almost furry02750533957028
0 Leaves not finely divided ; may have toothed or entire margins02750543958029
0 Plant forming strikingly pale whitish-green patches, with bi- or tripinnately branched shoots 5-12 cm long 028535540590Trichocolea tomentella0
0 Plant reddish-brown (or yellow, orange, or olive-green), with once pinnate to bipinnate shoots ; leaf lobes fringed with long teeth 028535640600Ptilidium ciliare0
0 Leaves 2-, 3-, or 4-cleft, more or less symmetrical02954574161045
0 Leaves simple and rounded, the margins either entire or with numerous, minute teeth02954584162065
0 Smaller lobe lying on top of larger lobe, distinct when plant in situ03047594263031
0 Smaller lobe under larger lobe, not visible when plant in situ03047604264038
0 Each leaf divided to near base into 2 narrow oblong elements ; very common on acidic banks, rocks, etc. 031596143650Diplophyllum albicans0
0 Each leaf divided to about 1/3 or less, the segments round or nearly so, not narrowly oblong ; habitats various03159624366032
0 Smaller lobe only marginally smaller than larger one 032626344670Scapania compacta0
