0 Shoots about 1 mm wide ; leaves with angle on back edge ; underleaves present 042828354870Lejeunea spp.0
0 Shoots about 2 mm wide ; leaves round, with no angle ; underleaves absent 042828454880Radula complanata0
0 Plant deep green when dry, vivid green when moist ; edges of many leaves curled upwards, giving shoots an untidy appearance from above 043808555890Porella platyphylla0
0 Plant usually reddish or brown, occasionally green ; leaf edges not curled upwards, so leaves look like neat scales04380865590044
0 Lobule as wide as long ; common on trees and branches, growing appressed to bark 044868756910Frullania dilatata0
0 Lobule much longer than wide ; frequent on rocks, where often grows appressed ; on trees and branches in western Britain, usually hanging loose from the bark 044868856920Frullania tamarisci0
0 Plants with a strong, peppery or must smell (some people cannot detect it ; if in doubt then look up these very common species) ; leaves 2-lobed04557895793046
0 Plants with no distinctive smell ; leaves 2-, 3- or 4-lobed04557905794047
